1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,913
You have three maps, some things, and two people.

2
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:10,030
What you don't have yet is a story that ties them together.

3
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:14,439
Today Pim wants her tablet back,

4
00:00:14,889 --> 00:00:17,063
the pump wants three fuses,

5
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:22,296
and one bad idea with a crowbar loses the whole game.

6
00:00:23,196 --> 00:00:27,543
Every bit of it is an answer in a room.

7
00:00:28,743 --> 00:00:33,961
A choice has a condition in front of it, and outcomes behind.

8
00:00:34,861 --> 00:00:37,904
You've used both since the third lecture.

9
00:00:39,704 --> 00:00:43,183
On a map there are two new conditions.

10
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:47,561
Holding asks what the person answering is carrying.

11
00:00:48,461 --> 00:00:53,243
Party asks what everybody on the ground is carrying between them.

12
00:00:55,043 --> 00:00:57,217
And there are new outcomes.

13
00:00:58,117 --> 00:01:02,900
Give and take move things in and out of a pack.

14
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,409
Open and reveal work on props.

15
00:01:07,309 --> 00:01:10,787
Calm, rouse, dismiss and summon work on people.

16
00:01:11,987 --> 00:01:14,161
First a quest that waits.

17
00:01:14,611 --> 00:01:16,785
It starts when it's revealed,

18
00:01:17,235 --> 00:01:20,278
which means when an answer says so.

19
00:01:21,178 --> 00:01:24,222
Lint warns that nothing reveals it yet,

20
00:01:24,672 --> 00:01:26,846
and that's true for now.

21
00:01:28,646 --> 00:01:31,254
Then two things that begin hidden.

22
00:01:32,154 --> 00:01:36,937
A second record for Pim, by the tent in the yard.

23
00:01:37,387 --> 00:01:42,170
When somebody goes somewhere else on a map, they're two records:

24
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:46,533
the one who leaves, and the one who arrives.

25
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:50,476
And a medical kit under a rock,

26
00:01:50,926 --> 00:01:53,535
hidden until a scene shows it.

27
00:01:54,735 --> 00:01:56,474
Now for her scene,

28
00:01:56,924 --> 00:02:00,402
and it's where most of today's words live.

29
00:02:02,202 --> 00:02:06,985
This answer is only offered if the party learned a fact,

30
00:02:07,435 --> 00:02:10,043
from the notice by the door.

31
00:02:10,943 --> 00:02:13,117
This one reveals the stash.

32
00:02:14,017 --> 00:02:17,930
In the next room, a promise accepts the quest.

33
00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:21,470
And here's the payoff.

34
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:25,833
It's offered only to the one holding the tablet.

35
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:30,211
Then three outcomes in a row, with commas:

36
00:02:30,661 --> 00:02:35,009
take the tablet, complete the quest, and give a fuse.

37
00:02:36,809 --> 00:02:38,983
There's a mean answer too.

38
00:02:39,433 --> 00:02:42,041
Keep the tablet, and she's roused:

39
00:02:42,491 --> 00:02:45,100
she attacks, and the quest fails.

40
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,174
And when she goes home,

41
00:02:48,624 --> 00:02:50,798
one answer dismisses her here

42
00:02:51,248 --> 00:02:52,987
and summons her there.

43
00:02:54,187 --> 00:02:56,796
The pump needs three fuses now.

44
00:02:57,696 --> 00:02:59,435
Look at the condition,

45
00:02:59,885 --> 00:03:02,493
and at the outcome after it.

46
00:03:03,393 --> 00:03:05,567
Holding three, and take three.

47
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:10,846
Take always takes from the person who answers.

48
00:03:11,296 --> 00:03:16,948
So the condition in front of it is always holding, and never party.

49
00:03:18,748 --> 00:03:21,791
The lines at the top are different.

50
00:03:22,241 --> 00:03:24,850
A line is read by everybody,

51
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,343
so a line asks about the party.

52
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:32,752
The second answer is a gamble.

53
00:03:33,202 --> 00:03:36,246
Two fuses and a bit of wire,

54
00:03:36,696 --> 00:03:39,304
and a roll that can fail.

55
00:03:40,204 --> 00:03:42,813
And notice where the signal went.

56
00:03:43,263 --> 00:03:46,307
Two answers lead to this room now,

57
00:03:46,757 --> 00:03:50,670
so the signal sits on its one way out.

58
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:54,913
The starter's terminal already teaches a fact.

59
00:03:55,363 --> 00:03:57,537
Give it a second use.

60
00:03:58,437 --> 00:04:01,915
Send the sentry its update, and it's calm.

61
00:04:02,365 --> 00:04:04,974
It keeps its power cell, though,

62
00:04:05,424 --> 00:04:08,467
so the party still needs another one.

63
00:04:10,267 --> 00:04:14,180
And Marrow gets one answer about the brass key.

64
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,820
That condition is party,

65
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:19,009
because nothing is taken,

66
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:23,372
and it doesn't matter who picked the key up.

67
00:04:24,572 --> 00:04:28,920
You wrote no Win line today, and no Lose line.

68
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:31,559
You didn't need to.

69
00:04:32,009 --> 00:04:34,617
Both sit on the starter's quest.

70
00:04:36,417 --> 00:04:38,591
Your crowbar fails that quest,

71
00:04:39,041 --> 00:04:42,954
so it loses the game from two maps away.

72
00:04:43,854 --> 00:04:47,333
And your spare cell is a power cell,

73
00:04:47,783 --> 00:04:51,261
so the starter's own winning answer takes it.

74
00:04:53,061 --> 00:04:54,800
One more word, discover,

75
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:57,859
tells the ship an area exists.

76
00:04:58,759 --> 00:05:00,933
It works in the game.

77
00:05:01,383 --> 00:05:03,557
But lint calls it unknown,

78
00:05:04,007 --> 00:05:07,920
so it stays out of your mission for now.

79
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,293
Play the long way round.

80
00:05:12,193 --> 00:05:15,672
The key, then Marrow, and then the gully.

81
00:05:16,572 --> 00:05:18,746
Pim asks for her tablet.

82
00:05:19,646 --> 00:05:24,428
The crawler, the tablet, and back to Pim for a fuse.

83
00:05:25,328 --> 00:05:27,502
Three fuses in the pump,

84
00:05:27,952 --> 00:05:30,996
then the gate, and the spare cell.

85
00:05:31,896 --> 00:05:35,374
Pim opens the relay house from her chair,

86
00:05:35,824 --> 00:05:37,563
and the beacon lights.

87
00:05:39,363 --> 00:05:43,711
Then play it again, and lose it with the crowbar.

88
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:50,293
For the exercise, give Marrow a use for the medical kit,

89
00:05:50,743 --> 00:05:54,657
and write a second losing answer that plays fair.

90
00:05:56,457 --> 00:05:59,935
That's the last new word for a while.

91
00:06:00,385 --> 00:06:04,733
Next time, the screen your crew has been looking at.
